module bindings.javascript.incomplete_key_denylist_guarded_read;

// A deep merge, deep defaults, or nested path walker that accepts
// caller-supplied keys usually routes every property read through one small
// helper whose whole job is to make those keys safe: compare the key against
// the prototype-mutating names, and otherwise return the property. The helper
// is what the rest of the library trusts, so whatever its denylist omits is
// reachable from every entry point that uses it.
//
// `__proto__` alone is not the whole denylist. Reading `object.__proto__`
// hands back the prototype directly, which is why it is the name everyone
// blocks first, but `object.constructor` reaches the same object one step
// later: for a plain object it returns `Object`, whose `prototype` the caller
// then merges or assigns into. A helper that returns the raw value for
// `constructor` therefore still lets a source object shaped like
// `{ constructor: { ... } }` mutate `Object` itself, because the caller
// recurses into the value the helper just approved. A complete denylist names
// `constructor` and `prototype` as well, or the helper checks that the key is
// the object's own property, which no plain object satisfies for either name.
//
// The binding is scoped to a value-returning helper — a function that reads a
// computed property and performs no dynamic property write of its own — since
// that is the form whose result the caller traverses. A single-level setter
// that blocks `__proto__` and assigns `obj[key] = value` needs nothing more,
// so a dynamic property write in the same function suppresses this.
binding incompleteKeyDenylistGuardedReadPrototypePollution {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "function" and node.context.language == "javascript" and node.context.prototypeKeyGuard == "true" and node.context.literal contains "__proto__" and node.context.index contains "[]" and not (node.context.dynamicPropertyWrite == "true") and not (containsAny(node.context.literal, ["constructor", "prototype"])) and not (node.context.prototypeNameGuard == "true") and not (node.context.ownPropertyKeyGuard == "true") and not (containsAny(node.context.callPath, ["hasOwnProperty", "Object.hasOwn", "Object.getOwnPropertyNames", "Object.create"]))
  emit issue code.IncompleteKeyDenylistGuardedReadPrototypePollution at node
}
